              "exact_label": false
            },
            {
              "kind": "css",
              "css": "[name=operator]"
            }
          ],
          "rationale": "The control has no accessible name, so role+name cannot address it at all. It is identified the way an operator does: by the visible label 'Operator ID:' in the same table row. A following-cell variant covers layouts where the label and control are siblings rather than row-mates. A structural selector on name='operator' is appended last: brittle by nature, but on surfaces this hostile it is sometimes the only thing left, and replay records when it is the strategy that had to be used."
